  "limits": [
    "Finite safety while receipts are retained; no liveness, fairness, unbounded theorem or Go/SQL refinement proof.",
    "One keyed request per scope, up to two clients/scopes and two digests; two-client runs allow two attempts, one-client run three. Concurrent contenders in several independent scopes together are not explored.",
    "PostgreSQL transaction atomicity, uniqueness arbitration, lock release and snapshot behavior are modeled assumptions checked against real PostgreSQL, not a proof of the database implementation.",
    "No digest/advisory-hash collision proof, HTTP authorization/canonicalization, receipt purge races, external callback effects, arbitrary delayed message histories or full server/process recovery.",
    "COMMIT acknowledgement fault injects EOF after real pgx Commit; paired precommit fault rolls back then returns EOF. No physical network fault proxy.",
    "The domain case uses actual Runtime management service and real PostgreSQL, with ordinary credential/holder test adapters and a fresh service object, not a process restart.",
    "No production defect established or production behavior/schema/API changed."
  ],
  "reopen_when": "Persistence and Runtime management owners revisit scope/digest/replay, transaction ownership, retry classification or receipt retention changes."
